#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0661.rst:323
msgid "Rejected Ideas"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0661.rst:327
msgid "Use ``NotGiven = object()``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0661.rst:329
msgid ""
"This suffers from all of the drawbacks mentioned in the `Rationale`_ section."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0661.rst:333
msgid "Add a single new sentinel value, such as ``MISSING`` or ``Sentinel``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0661.rst:335
msgid ""
"Since such a value could be used for various things in various places, one "
"could not always be confident that it would never be a valid value in some "
"use cases.  On the other hand, a dedicated and distinct sentinel value can "
"be used with confidence without needing to consider potential edge-cases."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0661.rst:340
msgid ""
"Additionally, it is useful to be able to provide a meaningful name and repr "
"for a sentinel value, specific to the context where it is used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0661.rst:343
#, python-format
msgid ""
"Finally, this was a very unpopular option in the poll [4]_, with only 12% of "
"the votes voting for it."
